        "body": "Dropbox is a for-profit, publicly traded company (ticker: DBX) founded in 2007 and headquartered in San Francisco, CA. The company describes itself as a provider of secure cloud storage, file sharing, and collaboration tools. Its platform supports synced team folders, previews for more than 175 file types, and a product called Dash, which the site describes as a way to save time and organize all company content in one place.\n\nOn the AI side, Dropbox offers a product called Dropbox AI, categorized under Notes, Knowledge, and Meetings, which provides document summaries, sharing controls, and integration with leading AI platforms. The company's site states that users can summarize content, create shared links, and save work back to Dropbox without switching tools, and notes that built-in AI summaries are described as coming soon.\n\nDropbox reported revenue of $2,521,000,000 for the period ending December 31, 2025, as disclosed in its 10-K filing. The company carries SEC CIK number 0001467623. No litigation or MCP server registrations are currently on record for the company in the site's held facts.",
